## Agent Flow

This project has the agent-flow workflow kit installed.

Every task starts with `/agent-flow`:

```text
/agent-flow <task>
```

When the user types `/agent-flow <task>`, run `agent-flow run "<task>"` from
the project root. When the user types `/agent-flow` with no task, run
`agent-flow status` from the project root; continue an active run with
`agent-flow continue` if present, otherwise ask for a task in the
`/agent-flow <task>` format.

The AI infers tier and phase depth from the task. Trivial fixes collapse to a one-question interview and a single slice; feature work expands phases. The chain pauses for user review at the spec/slice-plan handoff and resumes with:

```text
/agent-flow          # resume the active run
/agent-flow status   # show progress
/agent-flow abort    # cancel the active run (artifacts are preserved)
```

Command mapping: `/agent-flow status` → `agent-flow status`, `/agent-flow abort` → `agent-flow abort`.
Treat `/agent-flow` as a skill trigger, not as a shell path.

### Steering with natural language
- "treat this as a feature, deepen the phases" → escalate depth
- "redo the spec" → re-enter spec phase
- "decline this PR comment politely" → comment-decline branch

### Artifacts

Run artifacts live at `.agent-flow/runs/<run-id>/`. The chain advances when the previous artifact exists, so context loss does not lose progress.

### Memory / Lore

Lore in `.agent-flow/memory/lore/` is **auto-indexed, searched, and cited**.

- `/agent-flow <task>` searches the lore index using task keywords; matches are inlined into the `design` phase prompt as a "Relevant lore" block (with Constraint/Directive excerpts). Cite where they actually apply; do not fabricate citations.
- `agent-flow lore list` / `search "<query>"` — direct index access.
- `agent-flow lore compact [--apply]` — recommended every ~60 days. 4-tier compaction (dedup → stale-drop → weight decay → cluster reports). Dry-run by default.
- `agent-flow lore init <slug>` — scaffold a new lore file.

Lore schema: frontmatter (title/type/date/scope/weight/tags) + body sections `## Constraint`, `## Rejected`, `## Directive` (the three required fields).
